# What must NOT be published as a static asset.
#
# wrangler reads this file, not .gitignore, so anything present in the working
# directory at deploy time is a candidate — including files git never sees.
#
# media/ is the dangerous one. It holds ~109 MB of licensed clips that exist
# locally but must only ever reach users through the Worker reading the private
# R2 bucket. Publishing them as static assets would put the raw files on a public
# URL, which is the exact thing the ExerciseAnimatic licence forbids.
media
media-samples
*.mp4
*.webm
*.mov

# Toolchain, docs, and build config: no reason to be fetchable.
worker
tools
docs
node_modules
.git
.wrangler
.claude
wrangler.jsonc
package.json
package-lock.json
README.md
.assetsignore
.gitignore
